{
  "$comment": "Where information in embedded metadata corresponds to a STAC field. `embedded.path` is a path into a node of the format document (`*` matches any key or index); `nodes` restricts it to the root node or to node types. `stac.paths` are tried in order in the places listed in `stac.in`: the asset object, then the document that holds it (Item properties or the Collection). In STAC paths `{name}` is the node name and `{0}` the value of the first `*`. `same`: values should be equal; `converted`: equal after the named conversion; `related`: describe the same thing in different forms, compared by a reader. Conversions: `comma-list` (comma-separated text ↔ array of strings, order-insensitive), `datetime` (ISO 8601 instants), `epsg-code` (integer ↔ \"EPSG:<integer>\"), `gdal-geotransform` (GDAL text \"c a b f d e\" ↔ affine [a, b, c, d, e, f]), `number` (text or \"nan\" ↔ number).",
